	(text "DOT CLOCK AND CHARACTER CLOCK (DIVIDE BY 6)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5e8007c1-1a95-5324-a022-3ec6d08a9b1c"))
	(text "Q1 (9 MHz in BYTE) and three 74LS04 gates oscillate: DOTCLOCK. IC8 (74LS163: a synchronous clear) counts 0-5 and is\ncleared by the NAND of QA and QC: CHARCLOCK every 6 dots; QC (high for two dots) is the 6845's clock. A 74HC160, as the\n2005 drawing has it, clears at once and would divide by 5." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8051c373-b8b9-5d63-aa3e-585c5e82d008"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
